{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "central_D2_lon_periodic",
    "description": "Centered second derivative (per-degree diffusion / 1-D Laplacian) along longitude with periodic (wrap) boundary on the latlon grid — the physically natural rule for a closed zonal circle (global recipe: dlon_deg = 360/NLON; see grids/latlon/grid.esm). Compound match on D(D(f, wrt: lon), wrt: lon) at priority 10, so it fires on the whole second derivative before any plain-D rule could lower the inner longitudinal derivative (esm-spec 9.6.3 compound precedence); a PER-DEGREE operator (the physical eastward diffusion composes the (180/pi)^2 / (R_sphere coslat)^2 metric factors in the consuming equation — see grids/latlon/grid.esm; the full metric spherical Laplacian with cos(lat) weighting is a documented FOLLOW-UP, not this rule). Interior columns [2, NLON-1]: the imported 3-point centered stencil (f[i+1,j] - 2 f[i,j] + f[i-1,j]) / dlon_deg^2. The two face columns wrap explicitly, following the central_D_lon_periodic / cartesian upwind1_D_periodic precedent: i=1 gathers (f[2,j] - 2 f[1,j] + f[NLON,j]) / dlon_deg^2 and i=NLON gathers (f[1,j] - 2 f[NLON,j] + f[NLON-1,j]) / dlon_deg^2, so the scheme is the same O(dlon_deg^2) centered second difference at every column and conserves sum(f) exactly (each column of the operator telescopes to zero net weight). The face values are FULL-RANK aggregates (singleton output range on the lon axis) rather than the esm-spec 9.6.8 worked example's rank-reduced form, so every binding's simulator fills the (1 x NLAT) regions without rank promotion. `dlon_deg` is a free name resolving to the consuming model's zonal spacing variable (consumer-supplied geometry contract); the rule itself never assumes the global extent, but composing it with a non-closing regional grid is a modeling error — use a zero-gradient lon second-derivative rule there. Match scoping: the pattern is the compound `wrt: lon` twice plus the constraint `where: {f: {shape: [lon, lat]}}` (esm-spec 9.6.1), so it fires only on the second longitudinal derivative of a bare field declared over this grid's lon x lat index sets — not on any unrelated D(D(., wrt: lon), wrt: lon) reusing the axis name, and, under import-edge renaming (esm-spec 9.7.7), the wrt literals and the where shape follow the renamed axis together, so two latlon instances coexist scoped to their own meshes. The constraint requires a bare shaped variable; a consumer differentiating a compound inline expression must bind it to a declared lon x lat observed first.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:rule", "family:finite_difference", "grid:latlon", "op:D2", "axes:lon,lat", "order:2", "stencil_width:3", "bc:periodic", "spec:9.6.8"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 10.4 (centered differences on periodic domains) and Chapter 2 (the [1, -2, 1] second-difference operator)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "../stencils/central_D2_lon_interior.esm" }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "central_D2_lon_periodic": {
      "params": ["f"],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [ { "op": "D", "args": ["f"], "wrt": "lon" } ],
        "wrt": "lon"
      },
      "where": { "f": { "shape": ["lon", "lat"] } },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [[2, { "op": "-", "args": ["NLON", 1] }], [1, "NLAT"]],
          [[1, 1], [1, "NLAT"]],
          [["NLON", "NLON"], [1, "NLAT"]]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "central_D2_lon_interior",
            "bindings": { "f": "f" }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "i": [1, 1], "j": { "from": "lat" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", 2, "j"] },
                    { "op": "*", "args": [-2, { "op": "index", "args": ["f", 1, "j"] }] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "NLON", "j"] }
                  ]
                },
                { "op": "*", "args": ["dlon_deg", "dlon_deg"] }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "i": ["NLON", "NLON"], "j": { "from": "lat" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", 1, "j"] },
                    { "op": "*", "args": [-2, { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "NLON", "j"] }] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", { "op": "-", "args": ["NLON", 1] }, "j"] }
                  ]
                },
                { "op": "*", "args": ["dlon_deg", "dlon_deg"] }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
